MECHANICS THE LANE NEEDS TO KNOW (LD-19 says ONE utility that always emits `minmax(min(var(--token), 100%), 1fr)`, but the floor varies per call site):
- `composes:` copies a whole class; it cannot take a parameter. The parameter must ride in on a custom property that the consuming rule sets locally. Shape:
    /* styles/grid.css */
    .autoGrid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(var(--grid-min, 168px), 100%), 1fr)); gap: var(--grid-gap, var(--space-md)); }
    /* consumer */
    .grid { composes: autoGrid from global; --grid-min: var(--grid-min-poster); }
  This works because custom properties inherit and the consumer's rule wins on the same element.
- auto-fill vs auto-fit is a real behavioural fork in the inventory (10 auto-fill sites vs 4 auto-fit sites) and cannot be expressed by one class. Either two classes (.autoGridFill / .autoGridFit) or a second custom property is needed — a lane decision, but the inventory forces it.
- The stylelint rule must exempt this file. .stylelintrc.json is a FLAT config today (no `overrides` key), so the exemption requires adding an `overrides` block keyed on `apps/web/src/styles/grid.css`.
- ALTERNATIVE CONSIDERED AND REJECTED: putting the utility in globals.css alongside the `.nf-*` classes. globals.css:116-128 documents that those live there only because a separate not-found chunk caused unused-preload warnings — a route-boundary problem, not a precedent for utilities. tokens.css is also wrong: its header (:3-28) scopes it to custom properties, and it contains no selectors other than :root.
